% Goal

Implement and maintain `brain/api/api_plan_tracks.py` as the POST {add: [track_id], remove: [track_id], base_rev} in ONE rev-guarded write covering both selection.json and exclusions.json, returning the new rev and the resulting membership. Adds append at the end preserving existing order; an add of an already-present id is a no-op, not a duplicate. add and remove of the same id in one body is a 400, because the intent is ambiguous. Removes drop the id from the selection and from any active bunch; A BUNCH FALLING BELOW 2 MEMBERS DEACTIVATES WITH A NAMED WARNING, NEVER SILENTLY, and this module writes that journal entry using the structured ArchiveResult/MembersResult bunch_store returns (bunch_store is library-scoped and cannot journal). Calls transition_overrides.reconcile so a removal ORPHANS rather than deletes its transitions, and the note override is retained, so re-adding the track restores both. A stale base_rev is a 409 carrying changed_files.

% Product contract

- Preserve the exact public interface declared in `<pdd-interface>`.
- Treat the reviewed architecture description in this prompt as normative behavior.
- Keep plan identity, immutable track identity, revision guards, and non-destructive storage semantics intact across GUI, CLI, and agent callers.
- Preserve compatible behavior outside this module's stated responsibility; do not redesign unrelated mixing or playback logic.
- Reject malformed, stale, ambiguous, or unsafe writes explicitly instead of silently losing plan data.
- Keep the implementation deterministic where the contract describes deterministic behavior.
- Target Python 3.13+ for Python modules and baseline browser JavaScript without a bundler for browser modules.
- Inspect the current implementation, its declared dependency modules, and the focused tests before changing code. This is a brownfield source prompt: working, tested behavior not contradicted here remains part of the contract.

% Architecture detail

POST {add: [track_id], remove: [track_id], base_rev} in ONE rev-guarded write covering both selection.json and exclusions.json, returning the new rev and the resulting membership. Adds append at the end preserving existing order; an add of an already-present id is a no-op, not a duplicate. add and remove of the same id in one body is a 400, because the intent is ambiguous. Removes drop the id from the selection and from any active bunch; A BUNCH FALLING BELOW 2 MEMBERS DEACTIVATES WITH A NAMED WARNING, NEVER SILENTLY, and this module writes that journal entry using the structured ArchiveResult/MembersResult bunch_store returns (bunch_store is library-scoped and cannot journal). Calls transition_overrides.reconcile so a removal ORPHANS rather than deletes its transitions, and the note override is retained, so re-adding the track restores both. A stale base_rev is a 409 carrying changed_files.

